<title>USA: NORDIC SKIING-PICABO STREET SURGERY.</title>
<headline>NORDIC SKIING-PICABO STREET SURGERY.</headline>
<dateline>VAIL, Colorado 1996-12-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. downhill ski star Picabo Street had successful surgery to repair a ligament in her left knee on Wednesday her doctor said.</p>
<p>Street, injured in a training crash December 4, prior to a World Cup race in Vail, will be off snow for six months.</p>
<p>Dr. Richard Steadman, who performed the surgery, said Street, overall World Cup downhill champion the last two seasons, should be fit for the 1997-98 season.</p>
</text>
